<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="2f1cd51e-8143-4348-b6b6-55000302a21c" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">
    <introduction>
      <para>This is the documentation for IX.Libraries.</para>
    </introduction>

    <section>
      <title>Getting Started</title>
      <content>
        <para>To get started, add a reference to one of the NuGet packages part of the solution:</para>

        <list class="bullet">
          <listItem>
            <para>
              <externalLink>
                <linkText>IX.Library</linkText>
                <linkUri>https://www.nuget.org/packages/IX.Library</linkUri>
              </externalLink>
              - the base library that contains generic extensions and utilities
            </para>
          </listItem>
          <listItem>
            <para>
              <externalLink>
                <linkText>IX.Observable</linkText>
                <linkUri>https://www.nuget.org/packages/IX.Observable</linkUri>
              </externalLink>
              - a library that contains observable, view-model-like classes and utilities.
            </para>
          </listItem>
          <listItem>
            <para>
              <externalLink>
                <linkText>IX.Undoable</linkText>
                <linkUri>https://www.nuget.org/packages/IX.Undoable</linkUri>
              </externalLink>
              - a library for user-facing objects that need to be able to track and undo their changes
            </para>
          </listItem>
          <listItem>
            <para>
              <externalLink>
                <linkText>IX.Math</linkText>
                <linkUri>https://www.nuget.org/packages/IX.Math</linkUri>
              </externalLink>
              - a library that takes string values and attempts to interpret them as mathematical operations
            </para>
          </listItem>
        </list>

      </content>
    </section>

    <relatedTopics>
      <link xlink:href="6ba0616e-8c98-42ba-9c9f-2734fe0bc216" />
    </relatedTopics>
  </developerConceptualDocument>
</topic>